diagnosis_text:
Affected component: FRRouting (FRR) routing stack on router2, specifically zebra and bgpd. The management CLI (vtysh) depends on these daemons and fails when they are down.

Mechanism: With bgpd on router2 down, the eBGP session on router1 has no peer and sits in Active state, so router1 withdraws 200.1.1.0/24. As a result, packets from pc1 (195.11.14.0/24) toward pc2 (200.1.1.0/24) are immediately unroutable at router1, producing “Destination Net Unreachable” from 195.11.14.1. pc2 can still ping its default gateway (router2: 200.1.1.1), confirming local L2/L3 are fine.

Localization and evidence:
- router2: systemctl shows frr inactive (dead); vtysh fails (exit 1); frr_show_ip_route says “zebra is not running”; frr
